			"date": "2026-02-10T17:41:15.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> There’s a hierarchy.<br>A social media post(even in relatively unevil federated media) &lt; a blog(even in relatively evil Wordpress) &lt; a webpage(even if it wasn’t hand-coded)<br>I’m not sure if that’s a moral hierarchy, a hierarchy of tech arrogance, a hierarchy of “quality,” or some combination of the above, but I am increasingly unappreciative of the evanescence of social media. Quickly disposed posts promote disposable thinking. 🗑️</p>",
